\subsection{Hyperparameter Sensitivity}
\label{sec:sensitivity}

The adaptive method has two hyperparameters: quality threshold $\tau$ and ESS floor $\nmin$.

\paragraph{Quality threshold $\tau$.}
Table~\ref{tab:main} uses $\tau{=}0.7$ (recommended default).
At $\tau{=}0.8$, holdout PPL is comparable ($17.683 \pm 0.006$, $\Delta{=}{-}0.010$) but OOD improvements are substantially smaller ($\Delta{=}{-}0.005$ OWT, $\Delta{=}{-}0.004$ Wiki vs.\ $\Delta{=}{-}0.028$/$-$0.029 at $\tau{=}0.7$); $\tau{=}0.7$ outperforms $\tau{=}0.8$ in all 9 seed$\times$domain comparisons (Table~\ref{tab:tau}).
